        "text": "Under United States law, process uncertainty in food processing and agricultural engineering is directly codified in Treasury Regulation 26 C.F.R. § 1.41-4(a)(8) (Example 3), where a commercial food processor seeks to design a new fine-shred blade for a high-speed food processing line and evaluates numerous alternative blade geometries and metallurgical alloys through systematic trial and error to prevent product mashing and blade fatigue. Because conventional positive-pressure industrial blowers were mechanically inefficient and generated hazardous airborne shell dust during pecan cracking and separation, Nut & Co. engineered a vacuum suction-based <strong>Aspirator System</strong> (designed in 2012) for both small and large commercial shellers, conducting iterative aerodynamic modeling, prototype fabrication, and field functionality testing to eliminate design uncertainty and improve separation efficiency and equipment reliability under IRC Section 41."
