        "text": "This framework structures remediation across a five-stage risk lifecycle—(1) <em>Establish Context</em> (understanding the client's industry and audit history), (2) <em>Risk Identification</em> (using the Six-Eye team to locate claim weaknesses), (3) <em>Risk Analysis</em> (quantifying potential tax exposures), (4) <em>Risk Evaluation</em> (determining whether to claim a project based on a conservative risk philosophy), and (5) <em>Risk Treatment</em> (reconstructing documentation or removing marginal projects)—transforming ad-hoc error correction into a systematic risk-mitigation process for corporate CFOs and General Counsel."
