        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Successfully amending a prior advisor's bad claim must be paired with prospective compliance safeguards so that subsequent tax years do not suffer from the same substantiation failures. Under <strong>IRC Section 6001</strong>, <strong>26 CFR § 1.6001-1</strong>, and <strong>26 CFR § 1.41-4(d)</strong> (<em>Recordkeeping for the research credit</em>), a taxpayer claiming a credit under Section 41 <em>\"must retain records in sufficiently usable form and detail to substantiate that the expenditures claimed are eligible for the credit\"</em>."
