        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "First, from a statutory compliance standpoint, the enactment of I.R.C. § 174A under Public Law 119-21 (OBBBA) and the rollout of mandatory business-component-level reporting on Section G of the revised IRS Form 6765 have elevated the evidentiary threshold required at the time of filing. Taxpayers must maintain component-level records under 26 CFR § 1.41-4(d) and LAFA 20212501F that prove the Four-Part Test, substantiate the 80% process-of-experimentation and employee wage rules, and strictly exclude foreign research and international contractor costs under 26 U.S.C. § 41(d)(4)(F)."
