              "Contingent fees create a conflict of interest. Circular 230 § 10.27 restricts them on paper, but after <strong><em>Ridgely v. Lew</em> (D.D.C. 2014)</strong> it cannot be enforced for ordinary refund claims, and proposed regulations (REG-116610-20, Dec. 2024) would remove § 10.27. AICPA ET § 1.510 and state rules still bar CPAs from contingent-fee return and refund-claim preparation."
