        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Instead, the 2026 product documentation defines creditARMOR as a <strong>completely free, independent R&D tax credit mock audit simulation software service</strong> (requiring no credit card or subscription) covering <strong>39 federal and state programs</strong>—specifically <strong>1 U.S. Federal program</strong> (tracking the 4-part test, 20-year carryforward, and up to $500,000 annual <a href=\"/us/glossary/qualified-small-business-qsb\">QSB</a> payroll tax offset) plus <strong>38 state R&D tax credit programs</strong>: Arizona (AZ), Arkansas (AR), California (CA), Colorado (CO), Connecticut (CT), Delaware (DE), Florida (FL), Georgia (GA), Hawaii (HI), Idaho (ID), Illinois (IL), Indiana (IN), Iowa (IA), Kansas (KS), Kentucky (KY), Louisiana (LA), Maine (ME), Maryland (MD), Massachusetts (MA), Michigan (MI), Minnesota (MN), Missouri (MO), Nebraska (NE), New Hampshire (NH), New Jersey (NJ), New Mexico (NM), New York (NY), North Dakota (ND), Ohio (OH), Oregon (OR), Pennsylvania (PA), Rhode Island (RI), South Carolina (SC), Texas (TX), Utah (UT), Vermont (VT), Virginia (VA), and Wisconsin (WI)."
