          "<strong>The <a href=\"/us/glossary/asc-730-directive\">IRS LB&I ASC 730 Directive</a> and Contract Research Expenses:</strong> The IRS's official <a href=\"https://www.irs.gov/businesses/corporations/faqs-irc-41-qres-and-asc-730-lbi-directive\">FAQs - IRC 41 QREs and ASC 730 LB&I directive</a> explicitly state that <em>\"the Directive removes all contract costs from the computation of the ADJ ASC 730 FS R&D amount.\"</em> Under FAQ A4 on that IRS page, the removal of contract costs from the ASC 730 Directive safe harbor does not prevent a taxpayer from claiming eligible IRC Section 41(b)(3) contract research expenses on <a href=\"/us/glossary/irs-form-6765\">Form 6765</a>, but those contract research expenses are <strong>excluded</strong> from the ASC 730 Directive safe harbor and must be separately substantiated and remain subject to standard IRS examination procedures."
