        "text": "Under section 355-25(1) of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997, core R&D activities are experimental activities whose outcome cannot be known or determined in advance on the basis of current knowledge, information or experience, and can only be determined by applying a systematic progression of work. The government's program guidance at business.gov.au explains that a competent professional in the field must be unable to know or determine the outcome in advance from knowledge available anywhere in the world, without conducting the experiment."
