        "text": "For refund claims, The Tax Adviser (October 2025) reports that the IRS's 2021 requirements for <a href=\"/us/faq/irs-guidance-rd-tax-credit-refund-claims\">research credit refund claims</a> originally called for five items, and that a June 2024 update waived two of them at filing (the names of the individuals who performed each research activity and the information each sought to discover), leaving business components, research activities and total qualified employee wage, supply and contract research expenses required. IR-2025-99 also extended the transition period during which taxpayers have 45 days to perfect a research credit refund claim that the IRS finds lacking, through January 10, 2027."
