        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The case is <em>Jeffrey A. Harper et ux. v. United States</em>, No. 19-55933 (9th Cir. Feb. 25, 2021), 847 Fed. App'x 408, an unpublished memorandum disposition. The Ninth Circuit reversed a dismissal and held that the IRS, through a four-year audit directed at the taxpayer's research credit, had waived the specificity requirement in 26 C.F.R. §301.6402-2(b)(1). It was a taxpayer win on a procedural point. It did not impose new documentation requirements, although refund-claim specificity has drawn more attention since."
