        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Failed development work can count for R&D tax credits in the US, UK, Canada and Australia, and the official texts say so. In the United States, Treas. Reg. §§1.41-4(a)(3)(ii) and 1.174-2(a)(1) make success irrelevant to eligibility, while IRC §41(d) still requires the work to meet each part of the qualified research test. What decides a failed project's claim is whether the work, judged at the time, faced a genuine technical uncertainty and was carried out systematically, and whether records made at the time show that. For US filers, those records now also feed component-level reporting on Form 6765 Section G for tax years beginning after 2025."
