        "text": "<strong>Legal weight:</strong> Pursuant to IRC § 6110(k)(3), a Chief Counsel advice memorandum or Field Attorney Advice constitutes a written determination issued to internal IRS personnel and may not be used or cited as precedent. The binding legal obligation governing refund claim validity derives directly from IRC § 7422(a) and Treasury Regulation § 301.6402-2(b)(1), as interpreted by federal courts under the anti-surprise and administrative screening doctrines. Memorandum 20214101F, the IRS Research Credit Claims FAQs, and News Releases IR-2021-203 and IR-2025-99 represent administrative guidance and processing instructions detailing how the IRS evaluates compliance with Treas. Reg. § 301.6402-2(b)(1) at the intake and screening stage."
