        "text": "On June 18, 2024, following extensive practitioner feedback regarding the administrative burden of compiling employee-by-employee narratives at the initial refund filing stage, the IRS added FAQ 21 to its webpage titled Research credit claims (Section 41) on amended returns frequently asked questions. Under FAQ 21, the IRS announced that it waives two of the original five items of information required by FAA 20214101F: specifically, Item 3 (the names of the individuals who performed each research activity) and Item 4 (the information each individual sought to discover). This administrative waiver applies strictly to the threshold documentation that must be submitted with the amended return or refund claim at the time of filing to pass initial validity screening. The IRS explicitly cautions in FAQ 21 that both waived items may still be requested and required for substantiation if a research credit refund claim is selected for examination."
