    "summary": "Is a 30% R&D tax credit fee too high? For US businesses claiming the federal credit, a 30% success fee sits at the top of every published fee range and can far exceed the $7,500 to $50,000 cost of a study, especially on large claims. It is not unlawful as such, but audit-defense terms decide its value.",
