        "text": "While R&D tax credit consulting fees are negotiable in the open market, negotiating solely to shave percentage points off a contingent fee agreement is a false economy. In a federal enforcement climate defined by the PATH Act of 2015, the Inflation Reduction Act of 2022, the Form 6765 Section G business-component reporting rules (optional for tax years beginning before 2026 and mandatory for covered filers for tax years beginning in 2026 and beyond), and strict administrative and judicial enforcement of 26 C.F.R. § 301.6402-2(b)(1) in CCA 20214101F, Harper, and Premier Tech, Inc., the true economic cost of an R&D claim includes the latent financial exposure of an <a href=\"/us/glossary/notice-of-claim-disallowance\">IRS disallowance</a>. By selecting a transparent fixed-fee or Time and Materials structure with <a href=\"/us/faq/is-rd-tax-credit-audit-protection-worth-it\">contractual audit protection</a> and engineering-grade substantiation, corporate financial executives secure lower effective rates at scale without sacrificing compliance defensibility."
