        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "In <strong>Action on Decision (AOD) 2026-04</strong> (issued in October 2026), the Internal Revenue Service formally announced its Acquiescence in the decisions of both the Third Circuit in Mylan Inc. v. Commissioner, 76 F.4th 230 (3d Cir. 2023), and the Federal Circuit in <em>Actavis Laboratories FL, Inc. v. United States</em>, 131 F.4th 1345 (Fed. Cir. 2025). AOD 2026-04 specifically addresses the issue of whether legal expenses incurred by a generic drug manufacturer in defending Hatch-Waxman patent infringement suits must be capitalized under IRC §263(a) or are currently deductible under IRC §162(a)."
