              "<strong><a href=\"/us/glossary/substantially-all-rule\">Substantially all (80% or more)</a></strong> of the research activities for the business component (measured on a cost or reasonable basis) must constitute elements of a systematic process of evaluating alternatives (modeling, simulation, or <strong>systematic trial and error</strong> involving hypothesis, testing, data analysis, and refinement per Siemer Milling Co., T.C. Memo. 2019-37, and Little Sandy Coal Co., 62 F.4th 287). If the whole component fails the 80% test, the <strong>shrinking-back rule</strong> (§ 1.41-4(b)(2)) applies the test to the most significant subset of elements.",
