        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The procedural landscape governing R&D tax credit claims has tightened substantially following federal court decisions in United States v. Harper (847 Fed. App'x 408, 9th Cir. 2021) and Premier Tech, Inc. v. United States (No. 2:20-cv-890, D. Utah July 15, 2022), alongside the Tax Court's evidentiary rulings in Siemer Milling (2019), Little Sandy Coal (2021/2023), and George v. Commissioner (T.C. Memo. 2026-10). Under <strong>26 CFR § 1.41-4(d)</strong>, a taxpayer claiming a credit under Section 41 must <a href=\"/us/faq/documents-needed-for-rd-tax-credit-study\">retain records</a> in sufficiently usable form and detail to substantiate that the expenditures claimed are eligible for the credit."
