        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "First, for Research Credit <a href=\"/us/faq/amending-past-tax-returns-for-missed-rd-credits\">Refund Claims on Amended Returns</a>, Treasury Regulation § 301.6402-2(b)(1) requires that a refund claim set forth in detail each ground upon which a credit or refund is claimed and facts sufficient to apprise the Commissioner of the exact basis thereof. Under IRS requirements (IR-2021-203, effective January 10, 2022, as updated on June 18, 2024 in FAQ 21), taxpayers filing an amended return to claim an R&D credit refund must submit three mandatory elements upfront at the time of filing: (1) identification of all business components to which the Section 41 research credit claim relates for that year; (2) for each business component, a description of all research activities performed; and (3) the total qualified employee wage expenses, total qualified supply expenses, and total qualified contract research expenses for the claim year (which may be reported on Form 6765). Two previously required upfront elements—the names of individuals who performed each research activity and the information each individual sought to discover—were waived at the time of filing effective June 18, 2024, though the IRS retains the authority to request them during an audit."
