        "text": "Under the General Industry Average scenario (where the industry adjustment state parameter is set to 0.20), the financial model applies an expected post-audit adjustment risk of <em>a</em><sub>ind</sub> = 20% (0.20) to the gross credit value. Multiplying the $50,000 gross credit by the 20% reduction rate produces an expected post-audit credit loss (<em>L</em><sub>ind</sub>) of $10,000, leaving a net realizable retained credit (<em>C</em><sub>net, ind</sub>) of $40,000:"
