        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Current statutory and regulatory rules are more detailed. An election to use the ASC applies to the taxable year for which it is made and all succeeding taxable years unless revoked with the consent of the Secretary (IRC § 41(c)(4)(C); Treas. Reg. § 1.41-9(b)(1)). Under final regulations issued in T.D. 9712 (applicable to elections for taxable years ending on or after February 27, 2015), a taxpayer may make an ASC election not only on a timely filed original return (including extensions) by completing the ASC section of <a href=\"/us/glossary/irs-form-6765\">Form 6765</a> (Credit for Increasing Research Activities), but also on an amended return, provided the taxpayer has not previously claimed the IRC § 41 credit on an original or amended return for that taxable year and the period of limitations for assessment under IRC § 6501(a) has not expired for that year (Treas. Reg. § 1.41-9(b)(2)). However, a taxpayer that is a member of a controlled group may not make an ASC election on an <a href=\"/us/glossary/amended-tax-return-rd-credit\">amended return</a> if any member of the controlled group previously claimed the research credit for that tax year using a method other than the ASC (Treas. Reg. § 1.41-9(b)(2)). Once made, an ASC election may be revoked for a subsequent taxable year only with the Commissioner’s consent, which is automatically deemed granted if the taxpayer completes the Regular Research Credit portion of Form 6765 on a timely filed original return (including extensions) for that year; an ASC election may not be revoked on an amended return (Treas. Reg. § 1.41-9(b)(3))."
