        "text": "<strong><a href=\"/us/faq/failed-development-rd-tax-credit-eligibility\">Success is not required</a>.</strong> The section 174 regulation confirms that the ultimate success, failure, sale, or use of the product is not relevant to a determination of eligibility under section 174 (26 CFR § 1.174-2(a)(1)), and the credit regulation likewise does not require the taxpayer to succeed in developing a new or improved business component (26 CFR § 1.41-4(a)(3)). The costs still have to meet every other requirement of the test and the expense rules of § 41(b)."
