        "text": "Under the <strong>Immediate Interim Strategy (Capturing Contemporaneous Proxy Artifacts and Quarterly Surveys)</strong>, while transitioning toward comprehensive daily time tracking, management should configure existing project management and developer platforms (such as Jira, Git, or Tempo) to capture R&D evidence at the discrete business-component level as work occurs. Specifically, firms should maintain a master list of business components—recording each component's technical goal, start date, milestones, and completion date—and include the business component name or code directly in General Ledger entries and Jira/Git tags. First-line engineering supervisors and quality-assurance personnel supporting prototype building and testing should track their time by specific project rather than charging a single <a href=\"/us/glossary/general-and-administrative-functions\">General & Administrative (G&A)</a> or overhead code, ensuring the company can populate the direct research, direct supervision, and direct support wage fields on Form 6765 Section G. Furthermore, if real-time timesheets are not yet deployed, conducting <strong>quarterly time-allocation surveys</strong> tied to a current project list—combined with written baseline capability and uncertainty notes prepared by competent professionals at project kick-off in accordance with HMRC's <em>GfC3</em>—provides far stronger contemporaneous data than a single end-of-year survey and protects against data loss from staff departures."
