        "text": "Pursuant to Section 13206(e) of Public Law 115-97, this mandatory capitalization and amortization regime took effect for amounts paid or incurred in taxable years beginning after December 31, 2021. Under Section 13206(b) of Public Law 115-97, the transition from pre-TCJA Section 174 to TCJA-amended Section 174 was statutorily designated as a change in method of accounting initiated by the taxpayer under Section 446(e), made with the automatic consent of the Secretary of the Treasury, and applied strictly on a cut-off basis only to specified research or experimental expenditures paid or incurred in taxable years beginning after December 31, 2021. Because the statute mandated a cut-off transition, no adjustment under Section 481(a) was permitted or required for research or experimental costs incurred in taxable years beginning before January 1, 2022."
