        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Because Pub. L. 119-21 restored immediate expensing for domestic software development under Section 174A(a) for taxable years beginning after December 31, 2024, these capitalization effects after 2024 apply primarily to (1) foreign software development expenditures subject to mandatory 15-year amortization under Section 174(a), and (2) domestic software development expenditures for which a corporate taxpayer affirmatively elects amortization under Section 174A(c) or Section 59(e) specifically to manage its Section 904 FTC limitation, Section 250 FDII deduction, Section 163(j) business interest limitation, or Section 59A BEAT profile."
