          "<strong>Section G — Business Component Information (Lines 49–56, Optional for Tax Years 2024–2025; Mandatory Starting Tax Year 2026 Unless Exempt):</strong> Requires taxpayers to report granular project-level data for their top business components that account for at least <strong>80% of total QREs</strong>, capped at a maximum of <strong>50 business components</strong> displayed directly on Section G (with the remaining business components aggregated on an \"Aggregate\" line). For each reported business component, the taxpayer must provide: (a) the EIN of the controlled group member conducting the research, (b) the principal business activity code, (c) the business component's name or unique alphanumeric identifier, (d) the business component type (product, process, computer software, technique, formula, or invention), (e) for software business components, the software classification (<a href=\"/us/glossary/internal-use-software-ius\">Internal Use Software</a> [IUS], Dual Function Software [DFS], Non-IUS, or Excepted from IUS treatment), and (f) a disaggregated breakdown of QREs for that specific business component across direct research wages (Line 50), direct supervision wages (Line 51), direct support wages (Line 52), total wages (Line 53), supplies (Line 54), computer rental/lease costs (Line 55), and applicable contract research expenses (Line 56).",
