        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Regarding effective dates and small-taxpayer exemptions, the official IRS <em><a href=\"/us/faq/irs-form-6765-instructions-2024\">Instructions for Form 6765</a></em> specify that Section G was optional for all filers for tax years beginning before 2026 (unless filing an amended return claiming a research credit) and is mandatory for tax years beginning after 2025 (i.e., 2026 tax years and forward), subject to exemption criteria. In contrast, the official IRS <em>Instructions for Form 6765</em>—which carry controlling administrative authority—establish that a taxpayer is exempt from completing Section G if it either: (a) is a qualified small business (as defined under <a href=\"/us/legislation/26-usc-41h-payroll-tax-credit-qualified-small-businesses\">IRC § 41(h)(3)</a>) that checked the box to claim the reduced payroll tax credit, or (b) has total QREs determined at the controlled group level on Line 48 of $1.5 million or less <strong>AND</strong> average annual gross receipts for the prior three tax years of $50 million or less (as determined under IRC § 448(c)(3)), <strong>AND</strong> is reporting the research credit on an original return."
