        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Following an initial grace period that ended January 10, 2022, the IRS initially required five items of information at the time an R&D refund claim was filed. Effective for refund claims postmarked on or after June 18, 2024, the IRS waived the requirement to include two of those items—the names of the individuals who performed each research activity (or, under FAQ 10, the specific number and title/position of the individuals) and the specific information each individual sought to discover—at initial intake (though examiners may still request those two items if the claim is selected for substantive audit), requiring three core items of information at filing alongside the signed perjury declaration:"
