        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Primary legislative verification confirms that Section 10301 of the Inflation Reduction Act of 2022 (Pub. L. 117-169, enacted August 16, 2022) appropriated approximately $79.6 billion in multi-year supplemental funding through September 30, 2031—comprising roughly $45.6 billion for enforcement (approximately 58% of the total), $25.3 billion for operations support, $4.8 billion for business systems modernization, and $3.18 billion for taxpayer services—and contained no statutory headcount quota of 87,000 agents."
