    "title": "What triggers an R&D tax credit audit?",
    "description": "Claiming the federal R&D tax credit under IRC § 41 does not automatically trigger an IRS audit.",
    "summary": "Claiming the federal R&D tax credit under IRC § 41 does not automatically trigger an IRS audit. For U.S. businesses, audits typically stem from DIF scoring, random National Research Program sampling, and red flags such as disproportionately large credits, unexplained QRE spikes, amended-return refund claims (which the IRS screens 100%), industry code mismatches, and excluded activities.",
    "language": "en-US",
