        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The strategic analysis of Section 280C(c) reverses completely when applied to early-stage technology and biotechnology startups that utilize the <a href=\"/us/glossary/qualified-small-business-qsb\">Qualified Small Business (QSB)</a> payroll tax election under IRC Section 41(h). Enacted as part of the PATH Act of 2015, Section 41(h) permits startups with less than $5,000,000 in current-year gross receipts and zero gross receipts for any taxable year preceding the five-taxable-year period ending with the current year to elect to apply their generated R&D credit against the employer portion of their <a href=\"/us/faq/how-to-apply-rd-tax-credit-to-payroll-taxes\">payroll tax liabilities</a>."
