        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "IRC Section 280C(c) operates not as a mere ministerial checkbox on <a href=\"/us/faq/irs-form-6765-instructions-2024\">Form 6765</a>, but as a foundational balancing mechanism of federal tax law designed to prevent the double subsidization of commercial research expenditures. The legislative trajectory from the TCJA's mandatory capitalization regime—which inadvertently rendered Section 280C(c)(1) an exploitable \"excess\" anomaly during 2022–2024—to the corrective enactment of IRC Section 174A and the restoration of the full deduction disallowance under the One Big Beautiful Bill Act of 2025 underscores the financial significance of this provision."
