        "text": "Before any expenditure can enter the mathematical formulas of 26 U.S.C. § 41(a), the underlying research activity must satisfy the qualitative statutory definition of \"qualified research\" codified in <a href=\"/us/legislation/26-usc-41d1-qualified-research-definition\">26 U.S.C. § 41(d)</a> and Treasury Regulation 26 CFR § 1.41-4. Under <a href=\"/us/legislation/26-usc-41d2-business-component-test\">26 U.S.C. § 41(d)(2)(A)</a>, the four-part statutory test of § 41(d)(1) must be applied separately with respect to each discrete business component of the taxpayer."
