        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "While 26 U.S.C. § 41(a) applies uniformly to research conducted within the United States, Puerto Rico, and U.S. possessions, state legislatures have enacted localized R&D tax credit statutes that tether to IRC § 41 definitions while imposing strict in-state geographic sourcing rules, modified base-period formulas, and unique credit monetization options."
