        "text": "California conforms to IRC § 41 with significant statutory modifications codified in California Revenue and Taxation Code (R&TC) § 23609 (for corporations) and R&TC § 17052.12 (for personal income tax filers), administered by the California Franchise Tax Board (FTB) via Form FTB 3523 (Research Credit, Credit Code 183). California generally operates on static IRC conformity (referencing the Internal Revenue Code as of January 1, 2015, unless otherwise specified). Under R&TC § 23609(c)(2), both qualified research and basic research must be conducted strictly within California."
