        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "For <a href=\"/us/glossary/pass-through-entity-rd-credit\">pass-through entities</a>, S corporations compute the credit at 100 percent on Form FTB 3523 and transfer one-third (1/3) of the computed credit to Schedule C (100S) to offset their 1.5 percent entity-level franchise tax (or 3.5 percent for financial S corporations), while passing through 100 percent of the generated credit to their shareholders on a pro-rata basis. (If a C corporation had unused research credit carryovers upon converting to S corporation status, the carryovers are reduced to one-third for entity-level use, the remaining two-thirds are permanently disregarded, and the converted carryovers cannot pass through to shareholders.) Partnerships allocate the credit among partners based on each partner's distributive share as determined in a written partnership agreement under R&TC § 17039(e). Additionally, for taxable years beginning on or after January 1, 2024, and before January 1, 2027, California imposes a $5,000,000 annual cap on total business credit utilization per taxpayer or combined reporting group; taxpayers (excluding S corporations at the entity level) whose credits are disallowed due to the $5,000,000 cap may either carry over the disallowed credit (extending the carryover period by the number of years limited) or make an irrevocable election on Form FTB 3870 attached to a timely filed return to receive an annual refundable credit of 20 percent per year over five years beginning in the third taxable year after the election year."
