        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Using its $5,000,000 total current-year federal QREs and $4,000,000 prior three-year average federal QREs, Quantum Horizon computes its ASC base amount under 26 U.S.C. § 41(c)(4)(A) as 50 percent of the prior three-year average, which equals $2,000,000 ($4,000,000 × 50% = $2,000,000). Subtracting the $2,000,000 ASC base amount from the $5,000,000 current-year QREs leaves $3,000,000 in eligible incremental federal QREs ($5,000,000 − $2,000,000 = $3,000,000). Applying the 14 percent statutory ASC rate under § 41(c)(4)(A) yields a Federal ASC Credit of $420,000 ($3,000,000 × 14% = $420,000). Combining the $120,000 Basic Research Credit and the $420,000 ASC Credit produces a Gross (Pre-280C) Federal Research Credit of $540,000 ($120,000 + $420,000 = $540,000)."
