        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "For all non-exempt filers, Section G enforces the \"80% / Top 50\" Business Components Rule: taxpayers must list business components in descending order of total QREs until they account for at least 80 percent of total QREs reported on line 48, reporting no more than 50 business components determined at the controlled group level, with any remaining components reported on a single \"Aggregate Business Components\" line in column 49(c) (leaving columns 49(a), 49(b), 49(d), 49(e), and 49(f) blank and entering aggregate totals in columns 50 through 56). Filers using the <a href=\"/us/glossary/asc-730-directive\">ASC 730 Directive</a> enter \"ASC 730 Directive\" in column 49(c) with applicable Appendix B (column A) amounts in columns 53, 54, 55, and 56 (attaching Form6765ASC730AppendixA.pdf through Form6765ASC730AppendixD.pdf); if that single entry equals at least 80 percent of line 48 QREs, no additional business components need be reported in Section G. Filers using <a href=\"/us/glossary/irs-statistical-sampling\">statistical sampling</a> under Revenue Procedure 2011-42 must still report the 80% / Top 50 business components in Section G, adding the word \"sample\" to the component name in column 49(c) for sampled components and attaching Form6765StatSamplePlan.pdf."
