    "summary": "26 U.S.C. § 41(b)(2) defines in-house research expenses for the federal research tax credit: wages for qualified services, supplies used in qualified research, and amounts paid for the right to use computers. U.S. taxpayers whose activities pass the § 41(d) four-part test may include these costs at 100%, unlike contract research, which is generally limited to 65%.",
