        "text": "Under 26 U.S.C. § 41(b)(2)(D)(i), the term \"wages\" has the exact meaning given such term by 26 U.S.C. § 3401(a) for federal income tax withholding purposes. Consequently, eligible wages encompass all taxable remuneration for services performed by an employee for the employer as reported in Box 1 of IRS Form W-2, including base salaries, overtime, cash bonuses, and taxable stock option spreads upon exercise or disqualifying disposition. Conversely, the § 3401(a) definition excludes non-taxable fringe benefits (such as working condition fringes under IRC § 132(d) and § 3401(a)(19)), pre-tax 401(k) or cafeteria plan contributions, employer-paid health insurance premiums, and employer-portion payroll taxes (FICA and FUTA), even when paid to or on behalf of dedicated laboratory scientists performing 100% qualified research."
