        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "While <a href=\"/us/faq/state-vs-federal-rd-tax-credits\">state research tax credit statutes</a> overwhelmingly incorporate the federal in-house expense categories of 26 U.S.C. § 41(b)(2) (wages, supplies, and computer rental) and the § 41(d) four-part test, states impose strict geographic nexus walls, bespoke credit rate structures, and distinct IRC conformity dates."
