        "text": "While <a href=\"/us/faq/state-vs-federal-rd-tax-credits\">state R&D tax credit statutes</a> generally cross-reference the federal baseline of IRC § 41, state legislatures modify the base amount calculation in three fundamental ways: (1) adopting either static conformity (freezing IRC § 41 as of a specific historical date) or selective conformity; (2) restricting QREs strictly to research physically conducted within the state's geographic borders; and (3) redefining or eliminating the gross receipts multiplier in the base amount formula."
