        "text": "Under R&TC § 23609(h)(1), for taxable years beginning on or after January 1, 2000, and before January 1, 2025, taxpayers could elect the former federal AIC under IRC § 41(c)(4) (as in effect on January 1, 2015) using California's modified three-tiered rates applied against four-year average California gross receipts: <strong>1.49 percent</strong> on QREs exceeding 1.0% up to 1.5% of average gross receipts (Tier 1); <strong>1.98 percent</strong> on QREs exceeding 1.5% up to 2.0% of average gross receipts (Tier 2); and <strong>2.48 percent</strong> on QREs exceeding 2.0% of average gross receipts (Tier 3). However, under amended R&TC § 23609(h)(2), for taxable years beginning on or after January 1, 2025, California conforms to the federal <strong>Alternative Simplified Credit (ASC)</strong> election under IRC § 41(c)(4), modifying the federal 14 percent rate in IRC § 41(c)(4)(A) to <strong>3 percent (3.0%)</strong> of current-year California QREs exceeding 50 percent of average California QREs for the three preceding taxable years, and modifying the federal 6 percent fallback rate in IRC § 41(c)(4)(B)(ii) (where the taxpayer has no QREs in any one of the three preceding taxable years) to <strong>1.3 percent</strong> of current-year California QREs."
