        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Primary CRS and Treasury OTA publications demonstrate that this 4.5 percent figure does not apply to the Regular Research Credit under § 41(c)(2). Under the pre-2018 35 percent maximum corporate tax rate, electing the reduced credit under § 280C(c) multiplied the credit by 0.65 (1 − 0.35). As documented in CRS Report RL31181 and the Treasury OTA 2016 study, this reduced the unconstrained Regular Credit MER from 20.0 percent to 13.0 percent (20% × 0.65) and reduced the 50%-floor-constrained Regular Credit MER from 10.0 percent to 6.5 percent (10% × 0.65). Even after Treasury OTA discounted the constrained regular credit by an 82 percent realization factor to account for firms carrying unused credits forward, the effective rate was 5.3 percent (and in an earlier Tax Foundation example using a 34 percent corporate tax rate, the net effective rate at the 50 percent floor was 6.6 percent)."
