        "text": "Inspection of the statutory text of 26 U.S.C. § 41(c)(3)(B)(ii)(I)–(VII) shows that the transition phase spans five years (Years 6 through 10), does not blend the 3 percent rate into Years 6–10, and reaches full historical maturity in Year 11. Specifically, under § 41(c)(3)(B)(ii)(I), the FBP is fixed at 3 percent (0.03) for each of the taxpayer's first five taxable years beginning after December 31, 1993, for which the taxpayer has QREs. Thereafter, the FBP is computed as 1/6 of the aggregate QRE-to-gross-receipts ratio of the 4th and 5th such taxable years in the 6th such year (§ 41(c)(3)(B)(ii)(II)); 1/3 of the aggregate ratio of the 5th and 6th such years in the 7th such year (§ 41(c)(3)(B)(ii)(III)); 1/2 of the aggregate ratio of the 5th, 6th, and 7th such years in the 8th such year (§ 41(c)(3)(B)(ii)(IV)); 2/3 of the aggregate ratio of the 5th through 8th such years in the 9th such year (§ 41(c)(3)(B)(ii)(V)); and 5/6 of the aggregate ratio of the 5th through 9th such years in the 10th such year (§ 41(c)(3)(B)(ii)(VI)). In the 11th such taxable year and all subsequent years (§ 41(c)(3)(B)(ii)(VII)), the FBP equals 100 percent of the aggregate QRE-to-gross-receipts ratio for any five taxable years selected by the taxpayer from among the 5th through the 10th such taxable years, subject to the 16 percent maximum cap of § 41(c)(3)(C)."
