        "text": "Minnesota's R&D credit statute, Minn. Stat. § 290.068, subd. 2(c), defines \"base amount\" as \"base amount as defined in section 41(c) of the Internal Revenue Code\" (with Minnesota QREs and Minnesota-sourced prior four-year average annual gross receipts). In <em>General Mills</em>, the taxpayer argued that the statutory phrase \"as defined in\" incorporated only paragraph (1) of I.R.C. § 41(c) (because § 41(c)(1) uses the word \"means\" to state the product of the fixed-base percentage and four-year average annual gross receipts) and excluded paragraph (2) (the 50 percent minimum base amount limitation of § 41(c)(2))."
