        "text": "Furthermore, from a mathematical standpoint, a taxpayer with $0 California gross receipts claiming the Regular Research Credit under LDG 2012-03-01 and the § 41(c)(2) 50 percent floor receives a credit equal to 7.50 percent of its current-year California QREs (15% × (100% − 50%)), whereas electing the California ASC yields less than 3.00 percent of current-year QREs (or 1.30 percent if it lacked QREs in any of the prior three years). Thus, the 2025 California ASC is advantageous for taxpayers with positive California gross receipts whose calculated base amount under § 41(c)(1) eliminates or severely restricts their Regular Research Credit—not for $0 gross-receipts taxpayers, who achieve a much higher credit under the Regular Credit's 50 percent floor."
