        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Third, multi-state enterprises must maintain strictly segregated state-level Fixed-Base Percentage and gross receipts workpapers. Whether applying California's destination-sourced gross receipts definition and FTB Legal Ruling LDG 2012-03-01 zero-receipts 50 percent floor, electing between Texas Subchapter M franchise tax credits and sales tax exemptions, computing Georgia's three-year rolling ratio capped at 30 percent for payroll withholding offsets, leveraging New York's refundable Excelsior and Life Sciences credits, or navigating Indiana's historical substantiation standards, precision in state-specific base modeling is essential to defensible R&D tax monetization."
