              "Two or more organizations conducting trades or businesses owned by five or fewer persons (individuals, estates, or trusts). Under IRC § 1563(a)(2) for corporate groups, those five or fewer persons must possess <strong>more than 50%</strong> of the total combined voting power or <strong>more than 50%</strong> of the total value of shares of each corporation, taking into account each person's ownership only to the extent such ownership is identical across each organization. Under Treas. Reg. § 1.52-1(d) for trades or businesses under common control, the same five or fewer persons must satisfy both (1) the <strong>effective control</strong> test (<strong>more than 50%</strong> identical ownership across each organization in voting power/value, actuarial interest, or profit/capital interest) and (2) the <strong>controlling interest</strong> test (<strong>at least 80%</strong> aggregate ownership of voting power/value for a corporation, actuarial interest for a trust/estate, or profit/capital interest for a partnership)."
